WEBVTT

1
00:00:40.898 --> 00:00:42.483
Hey!

2
00:00:45.527 --> 00:00:48.197
Fry, mon, if you're going
to be living in the office,

3
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.324
you could at least
be on time for work.

4
00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:51.825
I'm sorry.

5
00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:54.203
I was up really late
poking through people's desks.

6
00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:58.290
All right, people,

7
00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:01.752
I will now outline
today's 12-point agenda.

8
00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:04.588
We'll begin with point one...

9
00:01:11.011 --> 00:01:13.055
...Concerning our pest problem.

10
00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:15.557
Somebody's
been leaving food around

11
00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.184
and it's attracting owls.

12
00:01:17.268 --> 00:01:21.480
And I, for one, am getting tired
of cleaning those owl traps.

13
00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:24.984
Now...

14
00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.278
As this shocking graph indicates,

15
00:01:27.361 --> 00:01:31.073
our water consumption
has tripled in the last month.

16
00:01:31.156 --> 00:01:33.867
Now, I notice
Fry has been here for a month

17
00:01:33.951 --> 00:01:35.619
so I'm appointing him
head of a committee

18
00:01:35.703 --> 00:01:37.246
to find
who's responsible.

19
00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:38.789
Fry?

20
00:01:43.294 --> 00:01:44.587
Am I cracking up

21
00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:45.671
or is Fry's living here

22
00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:47.464
starting to get in the way of bus...

23
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:55.556
What the hell are you doing?

24
00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:57.683
You're getting
a huge dose of radiation.

25
00:01:57.766 --> 00:01:59.518
And great lift.

26
00:01:59.602 --> 00:02:01.770
Do you know how long it's going to take me

27
00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:03.689
to recalibrate these engines?

28
00:02:03.981 --> 00:02:05.441
Hey, when you look this good,

29
00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.318
you don't have to know anything.

30
00:02:08.402 --> 00:02:10.446
Professor, we need
to talk to you about Fry.

31
00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:12.323
That's right!
We want some money!

32
00:02:12.406 --> 00:02:14.074
Wait, what's this about Fry?

33
00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:15.576
He's a nice guy

34
00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:17.870
but we think it's about time
he got his own place.

35
00:02:17.953 --> 00:02:19.038
Oh, fuff.

36
00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:21.123
He's not causing any trouble.

37
00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:23.834
Now, if you don't mind,
I'm rather busy.

38
00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:26.128
I seem to have mislaid
my alien mummy.

39
00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:29.548
This sarcophagus
should contain the remains

40
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:31.508
of Emperor Nimbala, who ruled

41
00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:34.428
Zuben Five
over 29 million years ago.

42
00:02:34.511 --> 00:02:35.804
Hey, professor.

43
00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.265
Mmm. Great jerky.

44
00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:39.433
Mmm.

45
00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:42.144
My God, this is an outrage.

46
00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:44.813
I was going to eat that mummy.

47
00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.107
Fry has got to go.

48
00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.321
Bachelor chow,now with flavor.

49
00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:54.406
...And bigfoot is down!

50
00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.450
Sheesh. 40,000 channels

51
00:02:56.533 --> 00:02:59.787
and only 150 of them
have anything good on.

52
00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.414
All My Circuits
is brought to you by...

53
00:03:02.498 --> 00:03:04.083
Robo Fresh.

54
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:06.627
Designed by a robot for a robot.

55
00:03:09.463 --> 00:03:12.883
I've been processing this
for some time, Monique,

56
00:03:12.967 --> 00:03:15.135
and, well... Will you marry me?

57
00:03:15.219 --> 00:03:16.303
Oh, Calculon!

58
00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:26.522
It fits!

59
00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:28.065
Then you must know that I'm...

60
00:03:28.148 --> 00:03:29.900
Metric? I've always known.

61
00:03:29.984 --> 00:03:33.362
But for you, my darling,
I'm willing to convert.

62
00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.244
Hmm, must be a friend of theirs.

63
00:03:40.327 --> 00:03:42.955
Fry, we've got to discuss
your living arrangements.

64
00:03:43.038 --> 00:03:44.623
We've all talked it over, and...

65
00:03:44.707 --> 00:03:45.916
Hey, All My Circuits.

66
00:03:45.1000 --> 00:03:47.334
Move over.

67
00:03:50.254 --> 00:03:51.380
Ah!

68
00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.507
Fry, sometimes in close quarters

69
00:03:53.591 --> 00:03:56.635
people do inconsiderate things
without realizing it.

70
00:03:56.719 --> 00:03:58.178
I know, but I forgive you.

71
00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.097
No, Fry, by "close quarters"

72
00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.223
I mean this office.

73
00:04:01.515 --> 00:04:02.641
Uh-huh.

74
00:04:02.725 --> 00:04:04.935
- And by "people," I mean you.
- Right.

75
00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.812
And by "inconsiderate,"
I mean...

76
00:04:06.895 --> 00:04:08.772
Leela,
we're trying to watch TV.

77
00:04:08.856 --> 00:04:11.483
Yeah. Would you kindly
shut your noise hole?

78
00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:15.738
So who's
that weird-looking guy?

79
00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.197
That's a human.

80
00:04:17.281 --> 00:04:19.241
- What's he do?
- Usual human stuff.

81
00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.369
He laughs, he learns,
he loves.

82
00:04:22.453 --> 00:04:23.871
Boring.

83
00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:28.208
Calculon?
I thought you were in a coma.

84
00:04:28.292 --> 00:04:30.461
That's what I wanted you to think

85
00:04:30.544 --> 00:04:32.421
with your soft, human brain.

86
00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:35.174
Hey, uh, why
is the TV getting smaller?

87
00:04:39.094 --> 00:04:40.804
We'll bill you for the couch.

88
00:04:47.895 --> 00:04:48.938
Cheer up, meat bag.

89
00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.648
You barely touched your amoeba.

90
00:04:51.273 --> 00:04:53.817
It looked good,
but I just don't feel like eating.

91
00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.654
- You want it?
- Nah, I'm trying to watch my input.

92
00:04:56.779 --> 00:05:00.574
I need plenty of wholesome,
nutritious alcohol.

93
00:05:00.658 --> 00:05:04.662
The chemical energy
keeps my fuel cells charged.

94
00:05:05.454 --> 00:05:06.622
What are the cigars for?

95
00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.415
They make me look cool.

96
00:05:09.124 --> 00:05:11.543
Oh, I can't believe
they threw me out like that.

97
00:05:11.627 --> 00:05:13.587
I must have been
really acting like a jerk.

98
00:05:13.671 --> 00:05:18.717
Yeah, but everybody's a jerk.
You, me, this jerk.

99
00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.469
That's my philosophy.

100
00:05:20.552 --> 00:05:22.972
So, where are you going to stay?

101
00:05:23.097 --> 00:05:24.556
I don't know.

102
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.142
Do refrigerators still
come in cardboard boxes?

103
00:05:27.268 --> 00:05:29.687
Yeah, but the rents are outrageous.

104
00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.355
Why don't you
just come move in with me?

105
00:05:31.438 --> 00:05:33.524
Really? That would be great!

106
00:05:33.816 --> 00:05:36.110
You sure I won't be imposing?

107
00:05:36.193 --> 00:05:38.487
Nah. I've always wanted a pet.

108
00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:49.498
Here we are, your new home.

109
00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.251
Cool. You know,
I've never even seen

110
00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:53.586
a robot's apartment before.

111
00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:56.130
Come on in. I'll give you the tour.

112
00:06:08.309 --> 00:06:09.977
Let's see, where to start.

113
00:06:10.477 --> 00:06:12.438
Okay.
This is the TV area.

114
00:06:12.521 --> 00:06:14.481
That over there is the breakfast nook.

115
00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.775
And over here is where you'll be living,

116
00:06:16.984 --> 00:06:19.945
which is great, 'cause till now
it's just been wasted space.

117
00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:21.739
It's kind of cramped in here.

118
00:06:21.822 --> 00:06:23.866
I don't even have room
to hang my clothes.

119
00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:26.160
Look, pal, you've only got
one set of clothes

120
00:06:26.243 --> 00:06:28.454
and you're not taking them off
while I'm here.

121
00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.291
Well, I'm bushed.
Good night.

122
00:06:32.374 --> 00:06:34.627
Wait. Bender? Bender?

123
00:06:38.422 --> 00:06:41.800
Kill all humans. Kill all humans.

124
00:06:41.884 --> 00:06:43.385
Must kill all...

125
00:06:43.677 --> 00:06:45.888
Bender, wake up!

126
00:06:47.056 --> 00:06:49.808
I was having
the most wonderful dream.

127
00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.644
I think you were in it.

128
00:06:51.769 --> 00:06:53.687
Uh... Uh, listen, Bender, uh...

129
00:06:54.188 --> 00:06:55.564
Where's your bathroom?

130
00:06:55.814 --> 00:06:56.982
- Bath what?
- Bathroom.

131
00:06:57.066 --> 00:06:58.567
- What room?
- Bathroom.

132
00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.652
What, what?

133
00:06:59.735 --> 00:07:01.445
Ah, never mind.

134
00:07:01.528 --> 00:07:03.197
Mmm...

135
00:07:07.743 --> 00:07:10.162
Hey, sexy mama...

136
00:07:10.246 --> 00:07:12.373
Want to kill all humans?

137
00:07:22.132 --> 00:07:23.968
We sure are cheerful
this morning.

138
00:07:24.051 --> 00:07:26.762
Yeah, this past week with Fry's
been a blast.

139
00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:29.723
You know, beneath his warm,
sunny exterior

140
00:07:29.807 --> 00:07:32.851
beats the cold, mechanical heart
of a robot.

141
00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.146
What happened to you?

142
00:07:36.438 --> 00:07:38.023
Oh, it's Bender's apartment.

143
00:07:38.107 --> 00:07:41.110
He put in carpeting yesterday
and now my head hits the ceiling.

144
00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:43.946
Hey, do you realize you're
standing at a weird angle?

145
00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:46.031
Now you're okay.

146
00:07:46.115 --> 00:07:47.950
Look at yourself, you're a wreck.

147
00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:50.369
You've got to find a new place to live.

148
00:07:50.452 --> 00:07:52.663
Is that an invitation?

149
00:07:52.746 --> 00:07:54.039
Love your optimism, Fry.

150
00:07:54.123 --> 00:07:57.459
But seriously, you've got to
tell Bender you're moving out.

151
00:07:57.585 --> 00:07:59.503
Yeah, but he might get kind of upset.

152
00:07:59.628 --> 00:08:01.463
I don't think I can do that to him.

153
00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.257
Hey, there's my little space heater.

154
00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:08.053
Well, I'm moving out.

155
00:08:08.137 --> 00:08:09.638
What?

156
00:08:09.805 --> 00:08:11.015
I'm sorry, Bender,

157
00:08:11.098 --> 00:08:13.058
but there's just not enough room.

158
00:08:13.142 --> 00:08:14.184
Not enough room?

159
00:08:14.268 --> 00:08:16.061
My place is two cubic meters

160
00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.606
and we only take up 1.5 cubic meters.

161
00:08:19.106 --> 00:08:22.067
We've got room for a whole
'nother two-thirds of a person.

162
00:08:22.359 --> 00:08:25.779
What if I just help the two of you
find a bigger apartment?

163
00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:27.281
I don't know.

164
00:08:27.364 --> 00:08:29.742
I've got a lot of great memories
in my old place.

165
00:08:31.201 --> 00:08:32.494
And now they're gone.

166
00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:40.586
Sure, it ain't one of them
la-de-da above-ground places

167
00:08:40.669 --> 00:08:44.131
but if you like dank...
Forget about it.

168
00:08:44.214 --> 00:08:46.300
At least it's got a great view.

169
00:08:46.967 --> 00:08:48.427
- Aah!
- What the...?

170
00:08:54.642 --> 00:08:57.061
'Scuse me. I got to go
change a lightbulb.

171
00:09:02.066 --> 00:09:05.027
Wow. Now, this
is fantastic.

172
00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.987
Hmm, I'm not sure
we want to pay

173
00:09:07.071 --> 00:09:09.198
for a dimension we're
not going to use.

174
00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:11.325
Aah! Ooh! Ee!
Ooh! Oh! Aah! Ee!

175
00:09:11.408 --> 00:09:14.578
Ooh! Aah! Ee! Aah!
Ooh! Ee! Ooh! Ee! Aah!

176
00:09:14.662 --> 00:09:16.121
Ooh! Ee! Ooh!

177
00:09:19.541 --> 00:09:22.169
Well, I give up.
What's the catch?

178
00:09:22.253 --> 00:09:23.379
Oh, no catch.

179
00:09:23.504 --> 00:09:25.798
Although we are
technically in New Jersey.

180
00:09:25.881 --> 00:09:28.467
Not one place even remotely livable.

181
00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:30.719
Oh, how awful.

182
00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.846
Did he at least die painlessly?

183
00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.932
To shreds, you say.

184
00:09:35.015 --> 00:09:37.768
Well, how is his wife holding up?

185
00:09:37.851 --> 00:09:39.687
To shreds, you say.

186
00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.105
Very well, then.

187
00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:44.900
Sad, sad,
terrible, gruesome news

188
00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:47.361
about my colleague, Dr. Mobutu.

189
00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:50.114
Was his apartment rent controlled?

190
00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:57.580
Wow. This is beautiful.

191
00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:59.665
What's with all the crap?

192
00:09:59.748 --> 00:10:01.000
It's not crap.

193
00:10:01.083 --> 00:10:02.626
Dr. Mobutu collected this crap

194
00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:06.297
while he was exploring
the whatchacallit... Universe.

195
00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.259
Well, this place has everything except
the only thing I care about... a TV.

196
00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:14.263
It's got a TV, you young
whatchacallit... Idiot.

197
00:10:15.598 --> 00:10:16.765
Ooh.

198
00:10:16.849 --> 00:10:18.058
Whoa, slow down.

199
00:10:18.142 --> 00:10:20.436
This place just
doesn't feel like home.

200
00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.229
It just isn't... Cozy.

201
00:10:26.191 --> 00:10:27.359
Ah...

202
00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.236
I can barely move.

203
00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.655
It's perfect!

204
00:11:21.163 --> 00:11:22.873
Man, it's a total sty.

205
00:11:22.957 --> 00:11:25.542
For the first time in 1,000 years

206
00:11:25.626 --> 00:11:27.253
I feel like I'm home.

207
00:11:27.336 --> 00:11:30.130
Yeah, it's going
to be fun on a bun.

208
00:11:30.214 --> 00:11:33.133
You know, Fry,
of all the friends I've had,

209
00:11:33.217 --> 00:11:34.510
you're the first.

210
00:11:39.974 --> 00:11:41.141
Hey, mon.

211
00:11:43.185 --> 00:11:44.937
Happy housewarming, Fry.

212
00:11:45.229 --> 00:11:47.314
It's a miniature fruit salad tree.

213
00:11:47.648 --> 00:11:48.649
Ooh.

214
00:11:53.821 --> 00:11:54.822
Wah!

215
00:11:54.905 --> 00:11:56.240
- Hey, Amy.
- Hey.

216
00:11:57.408 --> 00:11:58.742
This is for you, Fry...

217
00:11:58.826 --> 00:12:00.202
Zevulon the great.

218
00:12:00.286 --> 00:12:01.996
He's teriyaki-style.

219
00:12:05.124 --> 00:12:06.834
Wow. Heavy-drinking crowd.

220
00:12:08.252 --> 00:12:09.962
I'd better go out for more beer.

221
00:12:10.254 --> 00:12:12.590
Hang on. All My Circuits
is about to start.

222
00:12:12.673 --> 00:12:15.634
I know, but I need alcohol
to power up my batteries.

223
00:12:15.926 --> 00:12:18.262
If Calculon's wedding
doesn't go just right

224
00:12:18.345 --> 00:12:21.015
I'll be emotionally
and electrically drained.

225
00:12:26.687 --> 00:12:28.606
Hey...

226
00:12:33.694 --> 00:12:35.237
These are mighty tasty.

227
00:12:35.321 --> 00:12:37.740
Thank you.
I made them myself.

228
00:12:40.034 --> 00:12:42.244
Shh. The wedding's about to start.

229
00:12:42.328 --> 00:12:44.288
If anyone here objects to this union,

230
00:12:44.371 --> 00:12:46.749
let them speak now
or forever hold their...

231
00:12:50.753 --> 00:12:52.296
Is he objecting or backing up?

232
00:12:52.379 --> 00:12:53.964
Looks like both.

233
00:12:54.048 --> 00:12:56.258
I'm afraid
my half-brother is correct.

234
00:12:56.342 --> 00:12:58.260
You see,
I have a terrible secret

235
00:12:58.344 --> 00:12:59.345
and that secret is...

236
00:13:00.554 --> 00:13:01.680
Oh, come on!

237
00:13:01.764 --> 00:13:03.641
Oh, fix it.

238
00:13:03.933 --> 00:13:05.809
Hey, what happened to the TV?

239
00:13:05.893 --> 00:13:07.478
It just went out.

240
00:13:07.561 --> 00:13:10.022
This is an outrage.
I'm going to go yell at the manager.

241
00:13:11.899 --> 00:13:13.609
All right!

242
00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:15.736
Come back, Bender!
It's working!

243
00:13:15.819 --> 00:13:18.447
To reiterate,
my terrible secret is...

244
00:13:21.617 --> 00:13:23.035
It's out again.

245
00:13:23.118 --> 00:13:25.746
What? That's the last straw.

246
00:13:25.829 --> 00:13:27.915
It's back on!

247
00:13:30.918 --> 00:13:32.253
Pardon me.

248
00:13:32.336 --> 00:13:34.338
I don't mean to pry into
what you're doing in here

249
00:13:34.463 --> 00:13:36.465
with the crab and the one-eyed
lady and the Chinese girl,

250
00:13:36.757 --> 00:13:40.135
but everyone on this floor
is having trouble with their TV reception.

251
00:13:40.427 --> 00:13:43.013
Yeah, and you better
get rid of whatever's causing it

252
00:13:43.097 --> 00:13:44.556
or we're out of this dump.

253
00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.392
Relax, sonny.

254
00:13:46.475 --> 00:13:49.144
This cajigger'll find
the source of the interference.

255
00:14:06.662 --> 00:14:08.455
We want our TV back.

256
00:14:11.792 --> 00:14:13.502
There's your problem.

257
00:14:13.586 --> 00:14:15.879
Oh, my God.
Bender, it's your thingy.

258
00:14:18.299 --> 00:14:19.883
You people are nuts.

259
00:14:19.967 --> 00:14:23.387
My antenna never
interfered with my old TV.

260
00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:26.140
You had cable.
This is satellite.

261
00:14:26.223 --> 00:14:27.558
Obviously, your thoughts

262
00:14:27.641 --> 00:14:29.768
are being transmitted
on the same frequency.

263
00:14:29.852 --> 00:14:31.604
They're on my cell phone, too.

264
00:14:31.729 --> 00:14:34.315
Madame, I believe you're mistaken.

265
00:14:34.815 --> 00:14:37.526
Wow, that lady's got a huge ass.

266
00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.987
Those could be anyone's
thoughts, fat-ass.

267
00:14:41.447 --> 00:14:43.282
The robot has to go.

268
00:14:43.365 --> 00:14:44.950
Yeah!

269
00:14:45.659 --> 00:14:47.161
Well, you heard the mob.

270
00:14:47.661 --> 00:14:49.038
Fine. Come on, Fry.

271
00:14:49.121 --> 00:14:50.873
Let's move to that apartment

272
00:14:50.956 --> 00:14:52.124
that smelled like a sewer.

273
00:14:52.207 --> 00:14:53.876
You liked that one, right?

274
00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.377
Oh, it's tempting, but, well...

275
00:14:55.753 --> 00:14:57.504
I am already kind
of settled in here.

276
00:14:57.713 --> 00:15:00.215
Or we could live underground
with the mutants.

277
00:15:00.424 --> 00:15:02.843
A little fire'll show them who's boss.

278
00:15:03.135 --> 00:15:06.847
Uh... Listen, is there maybe
some way we could do this

279
00:15:06.931 --> 00:15:09.016
with you going and me not going?

280
00:15:09.099 --> 00:15:10.434
I don't understand.

281
00:15:10.517 --> 00:15:12.853
Well, you were going to
live in the closet anyway.

282
00:15:12.937 --> 00:15:14.980
Won't you be just as happy
back in your old place?

283
00:15:15.481 --> 00:15:18.025
But... Then
we wouldn't be roommates.

284
00:15:18.108 --> 00:15:21.070
I'll come visit sometime,
and you can visit me here.

285
00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:22.196
No, he can't.

286
00:15:22.488 --> 00:15:24.323
Anyway, I'm sure
it'll work out.

287
00:15:24.406 --> 00:15:26.367
This way we'll both be happy.

288
00:15:26.784 --> 00:15:29.245
Happy. Yeah, that's Bender.

289
00:15:29.328 --> 00:15:32.122
Always happy.

290
00:15:35.209 --> 00:15:36.752
Hey, the TV's back on!

291
00:15:37.461 --> 00:15:39.838
We are gathered to mourn

292
00:15:39.922 --> 00:15:41.298
the death of Calculon,

293
00:15:41.465 --> 00:15:44.385
industrialist, private eye, friend.

294
00:15:44.677 --> 00:15:47.221
Mind if I give the eulogy?

295
00:15:48.555 --> 00:15:50.808
Calculon! You're alive!

296
00:15:53.227 --> 00:15:55.521
Yay! Calculon's back!

297
00:15:57.606 --> 00:15:58.774
Right. So long.

298
00:15:59.066 --> 00:16:01.026
Good-bye.

299
00:16:01.235 --> 00:16:04.029
Do you think Calculon's evil twin
will ever walk again?

300
00:16:04.113 --> 00:16:06.532
I don't know, Amy.
I just don't know.

301
00:16:06.615 --> 00:16:09.034
- Wah!
- Hey, thanks for coming.

302
00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:12.538
Fry, you're Bender's best friend.

303
00:16:12.621 --> 00:16:14.623
How could you let that mob
kick him out?

304
00:16:14.707 --> 00:16:17.251
Aw, come on.
Bender loves mobs.

305
00:16:17.543 --> 00:16:19.545
Only when he's in them,
and you know it.

306
00:16:19.628 --> 00:16:21.213
You really hurt his feelings.

307
00:16:21.297 --> 00:16:23.299
Don't girl me with that girl stuff.

308
00:16:23.591 --> 00:16:24.925
Bender and me are guys.

309
00:16:25.009 --> 00:16:26.343
Guys don't have feelings.

310
00:16:26.635 --> 00:16:29.388
Bender's not a guy, he's a robot.

311
00:16:29.471 --> 00:16:30.973
Same thing.

312
00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.271
It's so big and empty.

313
00:16:39.773 --> 00:16:43.235
My roommate's gone,
and all he left behind was

314
00:16:43.319 --> 00:16:45.863
an eyelash
and three skin flakes.

315
00:16:52.703 --> 00:16:54.747
Aw... What's the point?

316
00:17:00.502 --> 00:17:01.629
Bender?

317
00:17:01.712 --> 00:17:04.006
My God, you're a mess.

318
00:17:07.092 --> 00:17:08.969
leave me alone.

319
00:17:09.303 --> 00:17:11.013
Look at that five o'clock rust.

320
00:17:11.513 --> 00:17:13.849
You've been up all night
not drinking, haven't you?

321
00:17:13.974 --> 00:17:17.311
Hey... What I don't do
is none of your business.

322
00:17:17.394 --> 00:17:19.396
Please, Bender,
have some malt liquor,

323
00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.274
if not for yourself, then
for the people who love you.

324
00:17:22.358 --> 00:17:25.527
I hate the people who love me,
and they hate me.

325
00:17:26.028 --> 00:17:27.279
Oh, now, look.

326
00:17:27.363 --> 00:17:29.615
It's obvious you miss being Fry's roommate

327
00:17:29.698 --> 00:17:32.284
but there's got to be a better way
to deal with this.

328
00:17:32.493 --> 00:17:35.454
Like how,
having my antenna removed?

329
00:17:35.537 --> 00:17:37.665
Well... If that would work.

330
00:17:37.748 --> 00:17:41.293
Are you crazy? That's little Bender
you're talking about.

331
00:17:41.543 --> 00:17:43.003
I can't cut it off.

332
00:17:43.087 --> 00:17:46.548
You're not a robot or a man,
so you wouldn't understand.

333
00:17:47.049 --> 00:17:48.759
I got to get out of here.

334
00:17:48.842 --> 00:17:50.010
Wait.

335
00:17:50.094 --> 00:17:51.804
I want you to look me in the eye

336
00:17:51.971 --> 00:17:54.056
and promise you won't
get behind the wheel

337
00:17:54.139 --> 00:17:56.892
without some kind of alcoholic
beverage in your hand.

338
00:17:57.351 --> 00:18:00.062
I promise nothing!

339
00:18:29.091 --> 00:18:30.634
I don't even want to...

340
00:18:30.718 --> 00:18:31.719
Why is...

341
00:18:38.392 --> 00:18:40.185
What up?

342
00:18:40.269 --> 00:18:42.771
I can't just stand by and be silent
about Bender anymore.

343
00:18:42.855 --> 00:18:46.275
Silent? You've been meddling
for two solid weeks.

344
00:18:46.567 --> 00:18:48.485
Well, I can't just do that anymore.

345
00:18:48.569 --> 00:18:50.487
Your best friend is out there somewhere

346
00:18:50.571 --> 00:18:51.655
destroying himself.

347
00:18:51.947 --> 00:18:53.449
Really?

348
00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:55.701
I didn't think he'd miss
this apartment that much.

349
00:18:55.784 --> 00:18:57.578
He doesn't care
about the apartment.

350
00:18:57.661 --> 00:19:00.497
He cares about you, and
you turned your back on him.

351
00:19:00.998 --> 00:19:02.374
Oh, man, I had no idea.

352
00:19:02.458 --> 00:19:05.294
If only I knew where he was,
I'd go talk to him.

353
00:19:06.962 --> 00:19:09.173
Oh, stupid TV.

354
00:19:10.382 --> 00:19:12.718
Bender.
You're blind stinking sober.

355
00:19:12.801 --> 00:19:15.220
That's right. I'm sober and crazy

356
00:19:15.304 --> 00:19:16.972
and I don't know what I might do.

357
00:19:17.056 --> 00:19:19.850
- Don't do it.
- I don't know what it is yet.

358
00:19:19.934 --> 00:19:21.936
Oh, yeah, now I remember.

359
00:19:22.019 --> 00:19:24.897
I thought I could live alone,
but I can't

360
00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:29.276
so I'm going to do what it takes
to be your roommate again.

361
00:19:29.568 --> 00:19:30.986
Bender, stop.

362
00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.572
Cutting Leela's head off
won't solve anything.

363
00:19:33.656 --> 00:19:36.242
No, I'm going to chop off my antenna.

364
00:19:36.325 --> 00:19:38.369
Hey... Yeah, that sounds good.

365
00:19:38.452 --> 00:19:39.703
Can I give you a hand?

366
00:19:39.787 --> 00:19:42.331
Fry, don't help him
mutilate himself.

367
00:19:42.414 --> 00:19:43.791
But it's a useless antenna.

368
00:19:43.874 --> 00:19:46.252
It's not like he's
a ham radio or something.

369
00:19:46.335 --> 00:19:47.461
I'm going to do it!

370
00:19:47.544 --> 00:19:49.630
I'm really going to do it!

371
00:19:49.922 --> 00:19:51.465
Don't try and stop me!

372
00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.218
Here goes!

373
00:19:55.344 --> 00:19:57.513
Ohh...

374
00:20:04.436 --> 00:20:05.437
Hey, it worked.

375
00:20:05.521 --> 00:20:06.563
The static's gone.

376
00:20:06.855 --> 00:20:09.400
I hate that this came
between us, Calculon.

377
00:20:09.483 --> 00:20:10.651
Me, too.

378
00:20:10.734 --> 00:20:13.821
I'm filled with a large number of
powerful emotions.

379
00:20:13.904 --> 00:20:15.489
You're my best friend.

380
00:20:15.573 --> 00:20:17.491
I'm sorry
I treated you so badly.

381
00:20:17.575 --> 00:20:19.034
Apology accepted.

382
00:20:19.118 --> 00:20:21.620
After all, you're only human.

383
00:20:23.956 --> 00:20:26.875
You guys could learn a
lesson from those two.

384
00:20:26.959 --> 00:20:28.085
She's right.

385
00:20:28.168 --> 00:20:30.296
You're my best friend, Fry.

386
00:20:30.379 --> 00:20:32.923
I'm sorry
I treated you so badly.

387
00:20:33.007 --> 00:20:34.466
Apology accepted.

388
00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:36.719
After all,
you're only human.

389
00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.597
Wait a minute.

390
00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:41.181
You did it all backwards.

391
00:20:41.682 --> 00:20:43.017
Fry's the one who should be...

392
00:20:44.059 --> 00:20:45.436
Oh, never mind.

393
00:20:49.023 --> 00:20:50.691
Oh...

394
00:20:50.816 --> 00:20:52.985
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

395
00:20:53.068 --> 00:20:56.947
I guess I'm just going to have to get
used to being half a robot.

396
00:20:57.031 --> 00:20:58.032
Aw, this isn't right.

397
00:20:58.115 --> 00:21:00.409
Listen, Bender, if
we found your antenna,

398
00:21:00.492 --> 00:21:02.036
could they still reattach it?

399
00:21:02.119 --> 00:21:05.915
Maybe, if we get it on ice
right away.

400
00:21:07.708 --> 00:21:08.876
Bingo.

401
00:21:08.959 --> 00:21:12.880
Hmm. You call
that an antenna?

402
00:21:16.842 --> 00:21:19.929
This time you'll have
all the human comforts.

403
00:21:20.012 --> 00:21:22.181
We'll get a couple of toilets,

404
00:21:22.264 --> 00:21:25.184
some food cookers,
maybe a puppy...

405
00:21:29.438 --> 00:21:30.689
It's good to be home.

406
00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:31.982
It sure is.

407
00:21:32.066 --> 00:21:33.859
By the way,
I saved your stuff.

408
00:21:33.943 --> 00:21:36.570
So that's where
those skin flakes went.

409
00:21:36.862 --> 00:21:38.656
Hmm. You think this fruit tree's

410
00:21:38.739 --> 00:21:40.199
going to get enough light?

411
00:21:40.282 --> 00:21:41.909
There's a window in the closet.

412
00:21:42.993 --> 00:21:45.955
Whoa.

413
00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.331
This is huge.

414
00:21:47.414 --> 00:21:49.541
Bender, why don't
I just live in here?

415
00:21:49.625 --> 00:21:51.543
In a closet?

416
00:21:51.627 --> 00:21:53.212
Oh, humans.

